{"name":"Biking Red","hex":"#7b222a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"biking","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act, process, or sport of riding a bike .","The act, process, or sport of riding a bicycle."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of bike"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biking"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cycling","blocks":[{"text":"Cycling, also known as bicycling or biking, is the activity of riding a bicycle or other types of pedal-driven human-powered vehicles such as balance bikes, unicycles, tricycles, and quadricycles. Cycling is practised around the world for purposes including transport, recreation, exercise, and competitive sport."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Cycliste_%C3%A0_place_d%27Italie-Paris_crop.jpg/330px-Cycliste_%C3%A0_place_d%27Italie-Paris_crop.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cycling"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg/500px-Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg/1280px-Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg/500px-Two_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Children riding a bike in Ghana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwo_siblings_on_their_way_home_after_school.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg/500px-Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg/1280px-Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg/500px-Cycling_kit_full_body.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACycling_kit_full_body.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Bicycle_emergency_repair_kit.jpg/500px-Bicycle_emergency_r